      "title": "Salmon bowls over couscous + cucumber, avocado, edamame (dressing from <a href=\"https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1022255-sesame-salmon-bowls\">Sesame Salmon Bowls</a>)",
      "do": "Couscous: boil 1½ cups water + salt; stir in 1 cup couscous; cover 5 min; fluff. Oven 425°; rub salmon with ½ tsp sesame oil + salt; roast 10–12 min until it flakes; break into chunks. Microwave edamame. Whisk ¼ cup soy sauce, 3 Tbsp white vinegar, 2 Tbsp canola oil, 2 Tbsp chopped scallions, 2 Tbsp minced ginger, ¼ tsp sesame oil. Bowls: couscous, salmon, sliced cucumber, avocado, edamame, scallions; drizzle dressing.",
